# Normalise line endings on checkout.
#
# `text=auto` normalises line endings INTO the repository but leaves the
# checkout format to core.eol, which defaults to `native` - CRLF on Windows.
# core.autocrlf does not change this; that setting governs the input side
# only.
#
# The repository already stores LF, so this changes no committed content. What
# it fixes is the working tree: a fresh clone had 205 of 301 text files checked
# out as CRLF, so any formatter or diff expecting LF reported whole-file
# changes that were not changes, and a Windows checkout and a Linux checkout
# held different bytes for the same commit.
#
# Naming eol=lf makes the working tree agree with the index on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.css linguist-vendored
*.scss linguist-vendored
*.js linguist-vendored
CHANGELOG.md export-ignore